  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}\\sqrt{1-{(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
